record templartorrent.evidence.resume-bitmap/1 : evidence {
    title "Resume bitmap trusts unchanged files and rechecks the rest"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:f1d59c5a23138dd76b7509100baf43a2ed10292e
    command "cargo test --offline --workspace -- --test-threads=8"
    summary """
        Ubuntu 26.04.1, i7-13700H, rustc 1.99.0, commit f1d59c5. cargo fmt on storage, engine, the rbit adapter and the application, then cargo test --offline --workspace -- --test-threads=8: 169 tests passed, 0 failed. That includes storage durable_identity refusing a replaced file, engine adopt_trusted skipping reads of trusted pieces and skipping a leased piece, five resume unit tests (unchanged files trusted, a changed file rechecked, missing barrier and short bitfield rejected, spare high bits and a file-count mismatch rejected, LSB packing), driver_resume_bitmap_trusts_unchanged_files_only (trusted 4, then trusted 1 and checked 3 after an Episode01 mtime change, then failed 1 after an Episode02 byte flip), the persist round-trip with a missing barrier loaded as untrusted, and the worker shutdown test that writes barrier 1 and on the next launch refuses barrier 0 with a visible note while the job stays complete. A following cargo test -p templartorrent-rbit-adapter --offline -- --test-threads=8 passed the adapter tests again, including the 26 driver tests. Preview tests and the release binary were not run.
        """
}

